	"$comment": "The cyberpunk skin's own golden cases (tools/check_nui_snapshots.py reads them after the windows' case files; docs/ui/AUTHORING.md \"Golden case files\"), for the window families that show hooks or effects: the dialog kit, the system menu, the taskbar, the minimap and the chat log; and no-effects (with colors on the messenger) for the messenger and the help, whose overlays draw gradients; no-effects for the loading screen (with reduced-motion: its board shows the frame's hooks), the empire select and the quest dialog, whose overlays draw gradients; no-effects for the costume and the equipment view, whose stages draw gradients (the window's own cases have the inventory's, the dragon soul windows', the character's skill page and the item tooltip's). reduced-motion: the hooks at rest (the corner pulses whole, the edge light out). reduced-effects: the media theme, which takes the scan layer, the edge light, the minimap's halo and mask, the HP ring's track and the scrim's blur off. no-effects: what a device without effects draws (gradients one flat color, no layer). colors: a violet accent and a cyan highlight, which recolor the neon edge, glow and holographic tint (the accent slot sets the skin's edge tokens), also on the gallery. switch: settled in modern-dark, then switched to cyberpunk with one update; it differs from the plain golden only where the corner pulse is (the hooks are new at the switch, so their motion starts there), which is why it is a golden of its own. backdrop: the modal dialogs over the synthetic world (docs/ui/snapshots/backdrop.png), blurred by the scrim. translucent: the panel opacity slot at 80 over the same world.",
